It is a compressed archived file, but it is not a Unix binary version --
those are never distributed, since the binaries vary from machine to 
machine.  This file probably contains the source code, and instructions
on how to make it on different machines (UNIX, DOS, Mac, ...).

The compress is fairly common, and I imagine you can probably find an
uncompress for it on any machine -- If you post here, telling what
kind of machine you have, I'll bet someone here would have a copy.

On a UNIX machine you could either do it in two steps:
   uncompress nethack3.1.2.tar.Z
   tar -xvf ethack3.1.2.tar

Or in one step:
   zcat xnethack3.1.2.tar.Z | tar xof -
